Q: How to Load an .aspx page in Div with jQuery in asp.net? A: <p>It should be as simple as this, unless I'm misunderstanding something. I'm assuming it's on the main page where the menu is.</p>
<p>FYI, using .ajax instead of the .post shorthand gives you much more control over the headers.</p>
<pre><code>$(document).ready(function () {


    function loadPage(formData) {
        $.ajax({
            type: &quot;POST&quot;,
            url: &quot;http://mywebsite/ExternalPage.aspx&quot;,
            data: formData, // { id: 1, name: 'Jim' }
            crossDomain: false, // ?? 
            dataType: &quot;json&quot;,
            async: true
            //old way....
            // ,
            // success: function (result) {
            //     $(&quot;#divExternalPage&quot;).html(result);
            // },
            // error: function (e, Msg) {
            //     console.log(`Error: ${e} : ${Msg}`);
            // }
        })
        .done(function(response) {
            console.log('Success!', response);
            $(&quot;#divExternalPage&quot;).html(response);
        })
        .fail(function(jqXHR, textStatus, error) {
            console.error('Request failed:', textStatus, error);
        });
    }

});
</code></pre>
<p>Also, I didn't test this. Not 100% certain the fail function is correct, but you get the idea.</p>

Q: Background image not filling page A: <p>The main issue is that your <strong><code>.bg-responsive</code></strong> has a fixed height of <strong><code>600px</code></strong>. If you want the background image to cover the entire viewport, use <strong><code>min-height: 100vh</code></strong> instead.</p>
<p>Try this:</p>
<pre><code>html, body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 100%;
}

.bg-responsive {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 100vh;
    background-image: url('img/main_top_header/0001_foundation_header_page.jpg');
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
}

/* Adjust height for mobile devices */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
    .bg-responsive {
        min-height: 100vh;
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>One other important point: you currently have:</p>
<pre><code>background-size: 100% 100%;
</code></pre>
<p>This forces the image to stretch to exactly the width and height of the container, which can distort the image.</p>
<p>Using:</p>
<pre><code>background-size: cover;
</code></pre>
<p>is usually better. It makes the image cover the entire container while maintaining its aspect ratio. Some parts of the image may be cropped, but it won't be distorted.</p>
<p>If you want the image to cover <strong>only the top/hero section</strong>, with the navbar and other content appearing normally underneath it, then you should use a slightly different structure.</p>

Q: JPA Cannot join to attribute of basic type A: <p>You are joined to attribute of basic type because you are join String &quot;category_id&quot;</p>
<pre><code>&quot;Join&lt;EntrepreneurCategory, Category&gt; categoryJoin = entrepreneurCategoryRoot.join(&quot;category_id&quot;,JoinType.LEFT);&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>You need to change to join to a category like:</p>
<pre><code>&quot;Join&lt;EntrepreneurCategory, Category&gt; categoryJoin = entrepreneurCategoryRoot.join(&quot;category&quot;,JoinType.LEFT);&quot;
</code></pre>
